+# NTSB radar correlation, production inventory and an FAA NTAP original
+
+October 27, 2026. Original-record work plan: recorder/radar/clock track, AUD016-A1 / TC01–TC04; related FAA clock-source follow-up. This unit acquired underlying source files and inspected their contents. It did not independently calibrate the clocks, recover a complete radar or audio CD or establish historical wrongdoing.
+
+## What advanced
+
+An **official NTSB-hosted 21-page radar study** now supplies the correlation method that earlier work only had through search leads. It uses adjusted RADES radar as the time reference, aligns FDR elapsed time through altitude using a single anchor, and describes checks with ATC radio callouts and FDR microphone keying. It reports a **+25.3-second radar correction** and a separate **New York NTAP correction of 8 seconds**. These are the report's stated corrections; the underlying calibration worksheets and fitted residuals are still missing. [Official PDF](https://www.ntsb.gov/about/Documents/Rec_Radar_Data_Study_all_aircraft.pdf), printed/physical pages2–4; [preserved copy](sources/Rec_Radar_Data_Study_all_aircraft.pdf).
+
+A **National Archives published FAA NTAP print file** was also obtained, with extraction commands, a tape ID, a nonfatal-looking warning and a successful program condition code, and coded time/position lists. Its chronological plot list yields **94 numeric-code entries** under two parsing methods. This is a real source-content test, not a test of actual clock accuracy or independent aircraft identity. [NARA7596008](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7596008); [preserved bytes](sources/NARA-7596008-1-ZID-48-ntap-AAL-9-11-01.txt).
+
+Finally, four page images of a **July 17, 2003 NTSB letter and February 21, 2002 inventory** identify more exact record targets: an AA77 RAPS projectCD, an ATC audioCD, FAA transcripts/tapes and an AA77/UA93 autopilot/navigation study. The letter says FBI authorized delivery to the Commission, with specified CVR exceptions. That assertion is not an independently acquired recipient receipt or proof that all named products survive. [Public reader](https://www.scribd.com/document/12962758/List-of-NTSB-Documents-Provided-to-9-11-Commission), reader pages1–4. The fifth page is a text-only locator here; its image and the native letter PDF remain unacquired.
+
