+## Timing statements and conflicting labels retained
+
+- **Radar standard and correction of +25.3 secondss:** page 3 says NEADS clock lagged other sectors by25.3 seconds, other sectors agreed with GPS, and25.3 seconds must be added to radar data from84thRADES. It says Washington/Cleveland/Boston NTAP needed no offset and New York needed8-seconds corrected. The paragraph does **not** specify the New York correction's sign. Preserve each source and correction separately. This verifies what the report states, not the calibration itself. It does not license applying25.3 seconds to our separate MCC audio derivative. ReadingRR03.
+- **Alignment and independence:** page 4 says FDR and ATC clocks were adjusted to RADES and describes one altitude-based FDR anchor, checked against radio callouts/microphone keying. This is affirmative methodological disclosure. An agreement after alignment is not automatically three independent measurements of absolute time. The actual per-recorder anchor values, match windows, drift analysis and residual/error tables remain missing. Do not claim an unperformed clock fit. ReadingRR04.
+- **EST versus EDT:** the same timing section specifies `HH:MM:SS Eastern Standard Time (EST)`, an anchor to `00:00:00 EDT`, and correlated local time`(EDT)`. Page 1 also labels subject times EDT. These words are preserved without selecting a controlling label or adding/subtracting an hour. A template/editorial issue and a processing/timebase issue are separate untested hypotheses; the native worksheet/settings would discriminate. ReadingRR04.
+- **Nominal sampling versus precise-looking labels:** page 2 describes ASR at approximately4½ seconds and ARSR at 12 seconds. These are reported nominal rates, not a guarantee of the completeness/accuracy of our selected file. Page4's±3,000-foot RMS statement concerns a particular radar-derived primary-height capability and AA11 discussion; it is not a universal height or timing error bound. ReadingsRR02/RR05.
+- **Display and processing context:** pages 5–10 name source-specific, combined, filtered and processed files, including `ZID bad NTAP.txt` and a `don't use D targets` filename. Those names are concrete retrieval keys, not evidence of dishonest filtering. Page 11 says FDR supplemented radar where available and solid/dotted lines mark time-window display conventions. The smooth map traces are not independently sampled paths. Its paragraph repeats United 175 where the report elsewhere includes United 93; page 4's comparison parenthetical appearsUAL83. These are preserved low-weight textual/label questions, not proof tracks or aircraft were substituted. ReadingsRR06–RR08.
+
+The exact identity of the **separately named Time Correlation Report** cited by the AA77 FDR report remains unestablished. This radar study contains a substantive Time Correlation section and refers back to FDR factual reports; the method is no longer wholly unacquired. Similar subject matter does not by itself prove this is the exact separately referenced artifact. Keep that join, its working files and original anchor values open.
+
+## NTAP internals: reproducible scope and numbers
+
+The original contains489 physical lines,16NULbytes, a terminalCtrlZ, one 0xb8 byte and four 0xb3 bytes. All bytes are retained. NARA's broad `ASCII Text` classification does not authenticate a strict 7-bit encoding. We use a reversible Latin1 display solely for analysis, without asserting the original character set. These formatting details are not evidence of alteration. ReadingNR01.
+
+Exact source lines20–40 and86 identify input tape`ID1635`; line 81 gives NTAP version`1.1-0 00.192`; line 93 selects codes`3743 6553`. Lines95–96 report a **FORMAT ERROR** on `ALTLIM`, while line 63 says the step executed with **condition 0000**. Both are preserved: successful termination does not prove every card was accepted; the warning does not prove every result invalid. The executable/control-card specification and follow-up log are needed to establish the effect. ReadingNR02.
+
+Lines97–98 request a plot from1234:00 but report tape start1234:32. Lines119–121 print a duration field`1409`, start1234:32 and stop1258:00. The endpoint subtraction is1,408 seconds; the duration field's units/inclusive convention are unverified, so we do not call this a one-second clock error. `DATE09/12/01` is a job/output field and is not assumed to be the flight event date. No 32-second deletion is inferred from the requested/available start fields. ReadingNR03.
+
+Only **LST3**, headed on line 381 and ending before LST4 at 434, was parsed. Each result retains the original line, column, byte offset, printed symbol/flag, code, rawALT, time, coordinates and matched source text:
+
+| Printed code | Entries | First–last printed labels | Successive interval distribution |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+|3743|80|1240:34–1256:19|72×12s;2×13s;5×11s|
+|6553|14|1237:43–1240:10|11×12s;1×11s;1×4s|
+
+These are **coded plot entries**, not 94 aircraft, 94 independent sources or a count of every original radar return. LST1/2/4 repeat or summarize output and are not counted again. Five fixed-point labels and one separate `D FIRE` plot row are preserved outside the numeric-code count. The wordFIRE is not established to mean a physical fire. Timezone, ALT units, exact aircraft association and clock calibration were not independently authenticated from this file. No correction of 25.3 seconds shift, clock fit or impact-time inference was performed.
+
+[Parser v2](inspect_ntap_v2.py), [94 retained rows and summary](NTAP-LST3-RESULT.json), [separate token/byte-span checks](NTAP-CROSSCHECK.json). The first parser run failed because **our control cited line 435 instead of 433**, and its boundary included three next-section header lines. Both mistakes were corrected in a separate version; expected values/hash and four controls were retained. [Failed v1](inspect_ntap.py), [failure record](PARSER-FIRST-FAILURE.json), [exact repair diff](inspect_ntap-v1-v2.diff). This is an analyst error, not a source discrepancy. The two methods then agreed on all 94 tuples and four source-row controls. These checks establish extraction reproducibility only.
