+## Production and record-location implications
+
+The letter's page 1 says the Commission sought raw radar and analysis, while NTSB limits its separate air-defense-response collection claim. Page 2 says FBI authorized delivery, excepting the UA93 CVR copy/early transcript draft; it directs CVR requests to FBI and says some delivered products incorporated FBI transcript information. Do not turn this into a claim that CVR information was wholly excluded or that no agency investigated air-defense response. Do not count the inventory and delivery letter as independent proof that every CD was actually received or survives. ReadingsRI01–RI02.
+
+Inventory page 1 gives **Cash / RAPS project CD**, **Gregor / ATC WAV CD**, **McComb/data tables/factual report** and **Ritter/flight-path study** for AA77. Page 2 gives **O'Call/Bower/UA93+AA77 navigation/autopilot report**, airline ACARS printouts, and the FAA transcripts/tapes box. Those item/staff/media descriptors are stronger retrieval targets than a general request for “everything about timing.” We have not acquired the identified CDs or the listed native working files. The last inventory page's Bower/radarCD rows remain text-only leads here, notwithstanding the separately acquired official radar study. ReadingsRI03–RI04.
+
+The inventory's **February 21, 2002** print date, the **July 17, 2003** transmittal and NPS's reported **February 2012** public release are different milestones. No decade-long delay, first-publication date or current withholding status follows merely from comparing them. The original 2003 receipt/enclosure verification and 2012 release packet are still missing. [Official NPS account](https://home.nps.gov/flni/learn/historyculture/flight-data-recorder.htm).
+
+## Next original records and falsifiable tests
+
+1. Obtain the original RAPS project/CD, agency tabular output, per-FDR anchor/clock worksheet and any separately titled Time Correlation Report. Reproduce the actual conversion with source version/settings, check missing/error-handled data, and preserve contrary results.
+2. Obtain RADES clock/GPS synchronization and event records, the signed New York8-second correction, ASR facility settings and native reference data. The reported correction can be tested only against those actual sources. Keep radar and audio recorder clocks distinct.
+3. Obtain NTAP version/control-card definitions and the tape ID1635 extraction package: establish ALTLIM/selection behavior, symbol/flag/ALT/time definitions, transform/filter rules and input/output completeness. NARA's finding aid separately lists source tapes, additional NTAP/DART files and audio; those entries are promising routes, not acquired payloads or proven byte-identical NTSB CD contents.
+4. Match independently identifiable altitude transitions, ATC callouts and FDR keying with their original clock references; predefine offset/drift and uncertainty criteria, retain residuals and avoid choosing events to force the favored impact scenario. A selected call/return pairing alone is not calibration.
+5. Obtain the Commission's actual delivery receipt/enclosure manifest, FBI release authorization and surviving-copy records. These can test the transmittal and completeness account without assuming either concealment or complete fulfillment.
+
+The strongest contrary consideration is that the newly obtained report **does disclose a concrete method and specific adjustments**. A previous implication that no correlation method was supplied must now be qualified. The remaining gaps concern the method's implementation, error bounds and original data joins. The observed text/label and command issues are review leads; none establishes a cover-up, false flight or conspiracy.
+
